{#
Day and week as a time-grid, for the calendar you own: hours down the side, an
event drawn where it is and as long as it is, and draggable.

**The grid itself is not here.** The gutter, the columns, the sticky headings,
the all-day band, the hour lines, the current-time line and the placement of a
block all live in calendar/_time_grid_shell.html.twig, which the public
shared-calendar page embeds too — the same arrangement _month_shell already has
with _view_month. What is left in this file is the only part that is about a
calendar somebody is signed in to: the drag controller, the chips that open an
editor, the "new event on this day" affordance, and the form and dialog a move
commits through. The shell's own header says why it is a shell rather than two
files that look alike, and what a caller may not put in it.

Reached from the full calendar page and from the docked pane alike: there is one
calendar here and the pane is a narrower window onto it, not a lesser version of
it. _grid.html.twig says why the pane no longer gets a list of its own.

Accepts (all from CalendarController::viewData):
  days    array<Y-m-d, list<OccurrenceCluster>>  — the day walk, for the keys
  range   the reader's answer; `grid` holds the placements, `zone` the clock
  view    CalendarView, for the field the move form posts back
  anchor  the date the view is centred on

**Double-clicking empty grid space creates an event there**, at the quarter hour
under the pointer. A single click deliberately does not, and that is the whole
reason it is a double: a single click on the background has to be told apart
from the end of a drag on every pointerup, and getting that wrong opens a dialog
every time somebody finishes moving a meeting. A double-click is unambiguous, is
what every other calendar uses for this, and needs no gesture arbitration at all.

The + button in each day heading stays, and is not redundant: it is the real tab
stop, and a double-click is not a gesture a keyboard has.
#}

{% embed 'calendar/_time_grid_shell.html.twig' with {
    dayKeys:    days|keys,
    grid:       range.grid,
    zone:       range.zone,
    today:      'now'|date('Y-m-d', range.zone),
    hourFormat: clock.hour,
} %}
    {% block grid_root_attributes %}
        data-controller="calendar--time-grid"
        data-action="pointerdown->calendar--time-grid#pointerdown
                     dblclick->calendar--time-grid#createAt
                     keydown->calendar--time-grid#keydown"
        data-calendar--time-grid-snap-value="15"
        data-calendar--time-grid-new-event-url-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_new') }}"
        data-calendar--time-grid-read-only-message-value="{{ 'calendar.grid.read_only'|trans }}"
        data-calendar--time-grid-pending-message-value="{{ 'calendar.grid.pending'|trans }}"
        data-calendar--time-grid-reverted-message-value="{{ 'calendar.grid.reverted'|trans }}"
    {% endblock %}

    {% block day_heading_actions %}
        <button type="button"
           data-controller="ui--modal"
           data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
           data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_new', { start: dayKey }) }}"
           data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}"
           aria-label="{{ 'calendar.event.new_on'|trans({ '%date%': dayKey|date('D j M') }) }}"
           class="w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-[10px] text-ink-faint
                  opacity-0 group-hover/day:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100
                  hover:bg-hover transition-opacity
                  focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent"
        ><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block all_day_entry %}
        {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with { cluster: entry, showTime: false } %}
    {% endblock %}

    {# The identity of what was placed, on the element the drag measures and
       moves. The shell owns the box's position and refuses to know what is in
       it; these are the caller's answer to "which meeting is this". #}
    {% block timed_entry_attributes %}
        {% set occurrence = entry.primary %}
        data-calendar--time-grid-target="block"
        data-event-id="{{ occurrence.event.id }}"
        data-recurring="{{ occurrence.event.isRecurring ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
        data-read-only="{{ occurrence.event.calendar.isReadOnly ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
        {# Wall time on the GRID's clock, which is the clock the drag is
           measured against and the one the move route reads the answer back
           in. #}
        data-starts-at="{{ occurrence.startsAt|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s', zone) }}"
        data-ends-at="{{ occurrence.endsAt|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s', zone) }}"
        data-instance="{{ occurrence.recurrenceId|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s\\Z', 'UTC') }}"
    {% endblock %}

    {% block timed_entry %}
        {% set occurrence = entry.primary %}
        {% set readOnly = occurrence.event.calendar.isReadOnly %}

        <div class="relative h-full rounded-md overflow-hidden
                    ring-1 ring-line bg-surface shadow-sm
                    {{ readOnly ? '' : 'cursor-grab' }}"
             style="background-color: {{ occurrence.event.calendar.color }}1a">

            {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with { cluster: entry, tall: true } %}

            {% if readOnly %}
                <i class="fa-solid fa-lock absolute top-1 right-1 text-[9px] text-ink-faint"
                   title="{{ 'calendar.grid.read_only'|trans }}"
                   aria-label="{{ 'calendar.grid.read_only'|trans }}"></i>
            {% else %}
                {# Mouse only, and aria-hidden on purpose: the keyboard route to
                   the same change is Alt+Shift with the arrow keys on the block
                   itself, so a focusable grip here would be a second tab stop
                   for a thing already reachable. #}
                <span class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-1.5 cursor-ns-resize
                             hover:bg-accent/40"
                      data-calendar--time-grid-target="grip"
                      aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block grid_footer %}
        {# The double-click's way into the editor.
           Hidden, and carrying the modal controller itself, because a Stimulus
           action only reaches controllers mounted on an ancestor and this one
           lives on #modal-backdrop — the same reason every chip carries its own.
           The grid writes the URL onto it and clicks it, which is exactly what a
           user pressing a + button does, so there is one path into the editor
           rather than two. #}
        <button type="button" hidden
                data-calendar--time-grid-target="newTrigger"
                data-controller="ui--modal"
                data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                data-ui--modal-src-value=""
                data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}"
                tabindex="-1"
                aria-hidden="true"></button>

        {# ── What the grid says back ───────────────────────────────────────── #}

        {# One hint, referenced by every block, rather than a title on each: the
           instructions are the same for all of them and a screen reader should
           not read them once per event. #}
        <p id="calendar-grid-hint" class="sr-only">{{ 'calendar.grid.keyboard_hint'|trans }}</p>

        {# role="status" rather than a toast. This is about the block the user is
           holding, so it belongs beside it and has to survive being replaced
           several times a second while nudging — a queue of toasts would not. #}
        <p data-calendar--time-grid-target="status"
           role="status"
           aria-live="polite"
           class="sr-only"></p>

        {# ── Committing a move ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}

        {# A real form submitted by the controller, not a fetch. Turbo then
           handles the answer exactly as it handles the editor's save — a full
           navigation to the redirect, which redraws the grid with the new
           placements. A fetch would need its own re-render path beside the one
           that already works. #}
        <form method="post"
              action="{{ path('app_calendar_event_move') }}"
              data-turbo-frame="_top"
              data-calendar--time-grid-target="form"
              class="hidden">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar_event_move') }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="timeZone" value="{{ range.zone }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="view" value="{{ view.value }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="returnTo" value="{{ app.request.pathInfo }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="eventId" data-calendar--time-grid-target="eventIdField">
            <input type="hidden" name="recurrenceId" data-calendar--time-grid-target="instanceField">
            <input type="hidden" name="scope" data-calendar--time-grid-target="scopeField">
            <input type="hidden" name="startsAt" data-calendar--time-grid-target="startsAtField">
            <input type="hidden" name="endsAt" data-calendar--time-grid-target="endsAtField">
        </form>

        {# The same question the editor asks, in the same words, because it is
           the same question — see EventMover. A <dialog> rather than the app's
           modal frame: this one is built from data already on the page and needs
           no fetch, and showModal() puts it in the top layer, which is the one
           kind of dialog backdrop-filter on an ancestor cannot clip. #}
        <dialog data-calendar--time-grid-target="scopePrompt"
                data-action="cancel->calendar--time-grid#cancelPending"
                class="rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface p-0 text-ink backdrop:bg-black/40">
            <div class="px-6 py-4 space-y-3 min-w-[18rem]">
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">{{ 'calendar.event.scope.legend'|trans }}</p>

                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="click->calendar--time-grid#commitInstance"
                            class="px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm text-left hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                        {{ 'calendar.event.scope.instance'|trans }}
                    </button>
                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="click->calendar--time-grid#commitSeries"
                            class="px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm text-left hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                        {{ 'calendar.event.scope.series'|trans }}
                    </button>
                </div>

                <button type="button"
                        data-action="click->calendar--time-grid#cancelPending"
                        class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                    {{ 'calendar.event.cancel'|trans }}
                </button>
            </div>
        </dialog>
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
